#[chapter/03/lore]{
  notes: [
    "The Off-Season Genie is a retired Discount Genie who liquidated his practice: grandiose wishes turned out to be cheap magic, and small honest wishes the expensive kind. The egg is the las..."
    "Wish-physics is karmic momentum: a wish doesn't create from nothing, it redirects momentum reality already has. Perfect version costs a miracle; mediocre version costs one coincidence and..."
    "The Genie can grant anything except see what Boof wants — her want sits below the resolution of instruments built for emperors. The low ambition fascinates him, and he joins the walk."
    "Two old routes wanting one turn settle for free under a traveler who asks nothing grander than a way through. The Genie recognizes his own trade performed by weather."
  ]
}

